{"data": {"notes": [], "reqs": [{"kind": "contract", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R1", "source": {"type": "task_metadata"}, "status": "active", "text": "Entry point `solve` in language python, within the stated limits.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R2", "source": {"char_end": 1283, "char_start": 0, "quote": "You are an expert Python programmer. You will be given a question (problem specification) and will generate a correct Python program that matches the specification and passes all tests.\n\n### Question:\nYou are given a string S consisting of digits.\nRemove all characters from S except for 2, and then concatenate the remaining characters in their original order to form a new string.\n\nInput\n\nThe input is given from Standard Input in the following format:\nS\n\nOutput\n\nPrint the answer.\n\nConstraints\n\n\n- S is a string consisting of digits with length between 1 and 100, inclusive.\n- S contains at least one 2.\n\nSample Input 1\n\n20250222\n\nSample Output 1\n\n22222\r\n\nBy removing 0, 5, and 0 from 20250222 and then concatenating the remaining characters in their original order, the string 22222 is obtained.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n2\n\nSample Output 2\n\n2\n\nSample Input 3\n\n22222000111222222\n\nSample Output 3\n\n22222222222\n\n### Format: Read the inputs from stdin solve the problem and write the answer to stdout (do not directly test on the sample inputs). Enclose your code within delimiters as follows. Ensure that when the python program runs, it reads the inputs, runs the algorithm and writes output to STDOUT.\n```python\n# YOUR CODE HERE\n```\n\n### Answer: (use the provided format with backticks)\n\n", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "The program is correct on all legal inputs of the statement.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R3", "source": {"char_end": 1324, "char_start": 1295, "quote": "Input:\n20250222\nOutput:\n222